          "content": {
            "tag": "H1",
            "font": "Poppins",
            "size": 48,
            "text": "Phonics is a method of teaching reading and writing by matching the sounds of spoken language (phonemes) with individual letters or groups of letters (graphemes). It acts as a decoder key for the English language.The 4 Core Pillars of PhonicsTo introduce phonics effectively, focus on these four foundational concepts:Letter-Sound Correspondence: Learning the specific sound each letter makes (e.g., the letter b represents the /b/ sound).Blending: Pushing individual sounds together to read a whole word (e.g., blending /c/ - /a/ - /t/ to say cat).Segmenting:",
